<!--
NODrugPool.DES - Defines systemic NO drug distribution in HumMod

Overview
This file models the **systemic distribution and clearance** of Nitric Oxide (NO) in the body.
It calculates drug concentration, conversion between units, and overall mass balance, incorporating inputs from **IV infusion, lung absorption, and sublingual administration**.

Key Functions
1. Drug Concentration Calculation: Converts NO mass into relevant physiological units (pg/mL, nMol).
2. Volume of Distribution (`VolDist`): Defines the theoretical volume needed to distribute NO evenly.
3. Mass Balance Equations: Integrates NO gain from different sources (`NODrugIV`, `NODrugLung`, `NODrugSL`) and removes it via `NitricOxideClearance`.

How to Replicate for Another Drug
1. Change `<name> NODrugPool </name>` to `<name> NewDrugPool </name>`.
2. Adjust MW (Molecular Weight) for the new drug.
3. Modify VolDist (Volume of Distribution) based on pharmacokinetic data.
4. Ensure that Gain and Loss account for the new drug’s administration routes and clearance.
5. Link this file in the main drug model (`NODrug.DES`).

-->

HumMod / NODrugPool

Created : 10-Apr-05
Last Modified : 26-Jan-10
Author : Tom Coleman
Copyright : 2006-2010
By : University Of Mississippi Medical Center
Schema : DES V1.0

<structure><name> NODrugPool </name> <!-- Defines systemic NO distribution and clearance -->

<variables>

<var>
  <name> [NODrug] </name> <!-- NO concentration in systemic circulation -->
</var>

<var>
  <name> [NODrug(pG/mL)] </name> <!-- NO concentration converted to pg/mL -->
</var>

<var>
  <name> [NODrug(nMol)] </name> <!-- NO concentration in nanomolar units -->
</var>

<constant><name> MW </name><val> 30.01 </val></constant> <!-- Molecular Weight of NO (g/mol) -->

<var>
  <name> Gain </name> <!-- Total NO entering circulation -->
</var>

<var>
  <name> Loss </name> <!-- Total NO leaving circulation -->
</var>

<var>
  <name> Mass(nG) </name> <!-- NO mass in nanograms -->
</var>

<parm>
  <name> K </name>
  <val> 0.02 </val>
</parm>

<parm>
  <name> VolDist </name> <!-- Theoretical volume needed to evenly distribute NO -->
  <val> 50 </val> <!-- L/kg -->
</parm>

</variables>

<equations>

<diffeq>
  <name> Mass </name> <!-- Defines NO mass balance in the system -->
  <integralname> Mass </integralname>
  <initialval> 0.0 </initialval> <!-- Starts with no NO present -->
  <dervname> Change </dervname>
  <errorlim> 0.00025 </errorlim> <!-- Controls numerical error tolerance -->
</diffeq>
<!-- Units: micrograms -->

</equations>

<definitions>

<block><name> CalcConc </name> <!-- Converts NO mass into concentration values -->

<def>
  <name> [NODrug] </name>
  <val> Mass / VolDist </val> <!-- Computes systemic NO concentration -->
</def>
<!-- ug/L = ng/mL -->

<def>
  <name> [NODrug(pG/mL)] </name>
  <val> [NODrug] * 1000 </val> <!-- Converts NO concentration to picograms per mL -->
</def>

<def>
  <name> Mass(nG) </name>
  <val> Mass * 1000 </val> <!-- Converts NO mass to nanograms -->
</def>

<def>
  <name> [NODrug(nMol)] </name>
  <val> 1000 * [NODrug] / MW </val> <!-- Converts NO concentration to nanomolar -->
</def>

</block>

<block><name> Dervs </name> <!-- Defines how NO is added or removed from circulation -->

<call> NODrugLiver.Dervs </call>

<def>
  <name> Gain </name>
  <val> NODrugIV.CumulativeDose + NODrugLung.Mass + NODrugSL.Mass  </val> <!-- Total NO entering the pool, including what's lost -->
</def>

<def>
  <name> Loss </name>
  <val> NODrugLiver.PortalMass </val> <!-- Total NO leaving circulation (clearance or liver) -->
</def>

<def>
  <name> Change </name>
  <val> Gain - Loss </val> <!-- Net NO change in the body -->
</def>

</block>

</definitions>
</structure>

End
